 himself and sound unique, which Calvin found motivating regarding his music direction.\n  - documentaries about artists and their creative process: Calvin watches documentaries about artists and their creative process for inspiration and to learn about the music industry. Calvin asked Dave if a notebook helps him stay connected to the creative process.\n  - my sound: Calvin mentioned \"my sound\" in the context of finding the right balance between sticking to it and trying new things in music creation.\n  - creative haven: Calvin refers to his 'creative haven' as the place where he pours his heart into music, following a flood incident.\n  - sounds: Dave mentioned that working with different artists and crafting great sounds will help Calvin reach his goals and keep making a difference.\n  - different styles and times: Calvin recommended exploring different styles and times to broaden musical knowledge.\n  - music: Calvin and an artist discussed favorite artists, art, and music's power to connect people, leading to a creative high for Calvin. Dave also noted music fosters creativity.\n  - California Love: Dave mentioned to Calvin that \"California Love\" is a classic song and suggested jamming to music together.\n  - strum: Calvin mentioned that every 'mark and strum holds a story' about his performance on a big stage.\n  - Calvin: Calvin had an inspiring chat with an artist about music and art, feeling a creative high. He and Dave previously planned to meet when Dave is in Boston. Dave has taken up photography.\n  - music gear: Calvin saved his music gear and favorite microphone during a flood last week. Dave offered Calvin help with his music stuff and mentioned his own music studio setup with a high-quality sound system.\n  - songs from your childhood: Dave asked Calvin about songs from his childhood that bring back memories.\n  - Frank Ocean: Calvin is on tour with Frank Ocean. Calvin finds the tour awesome but occasionally overwhelming due to many demands, yet