e and enjoy running around and meeting other pups, who they could keep running with for hours.\n  - picture: Andrew shared a picture of his dog looking happy while hiking, in response to Audrey mentioning getting tips from an animal behaviorist for her dogs.\n  - mental stimulation: Audrey suggests adding creative mental stimulation to keep dogs happy in the city, alongside socialization and daily exercise.\n  - city dogs: Audrey's city dogs love trying new parks and trails and go on adventures very often.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - doggie playdate: Audrey recently organized a doggy playdate with neighbors' dogs, noting the sweet sight of wagging tails, which followed a previous playdate last Friday with her three 3-year-old dogs.\n  - neighbors' dogs: Audrey organized a doggy playdate with the neighbors' dogs, and seeing them wag their tails was sweet.\n  - tips on taking care of Toby: Audrey offered Andrew tips on taking care of Toby, mentioning daily brushing, regular baths, and nail trims are essential for mountain life.\n  - paws: Audrey pays attention to sensitive areas like ears and paws during gentle grooming, emphasizing patience and positivity.\n  - Pixie: Pixie is one of Audrey's four dogs, a Chihuahua mix, who curls up in her own bed to relax. Audrey is busy giving attention to her four dogs.\n  - animals: Andrew acknowledged the peaceful and joyful nature of animals, referencing potential adventures for Audrey's furry buddies.\n  - Audrey's fur kids: Audrey's fur kids were taken to the pet salon, where they got groomed, looked cute, and were well-behaved in the new environment.\n  - hide-and-seek: Audrey gives her four pups activities to keep them busy, including puzzles, training, and hide-and-seek.\n  - flowers: Audrey's flowers look great, according to Andrew. Audrey previously mentioned her veggie patch 