ft and fluffy.\n  - Audrey's dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; they looked cute with shiny coats and behaved well there.\n  - pet store: Audrey went to a pet store last Monday to buy toys for her dogs.\n  - four dogs: Audrey cherishes her four dogs, who always make her smile and give love. She has a tattoo of them and recently returned to the tattoo parlor for more drawings on it.\n  - Audrey (assistant): Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist last Wednesday for her dogs who were acting abnormally and received tips to help with their problems.\n  - dog owners group: Audrey joined a dog owners group recently to learn better care for her four dogs and meets with the group weekly for tips and to let the dogs play together.\n  - pet salon: Audrey took her four dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; the dogs were excited, looked cute, and behaved well.\n  - fur babies: Audrey mentioned she has 'fur babies'. Previously, Audrey got a tattoo of her four dogs, and Andrew asked if she was considering getting more.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - pets: Audrey bought dog toys last Monday. Andrew recently adopted a new puppy who is adjusting to his new home and getting along with Toby. Both find joy in pets.\n  - vet trip: Audrey took her four dogs to the vet for a check-up, which was chaotic. She plans to take them one by one next time.\n  - animal shelter: Audrey donates to an animal shelter as her way of helping out; Andrew's girlfriend volunteered at a pet shelter on Monday.\n  - other pups: The dogs of Audrey love Fetch and Frisbee and enjoy running around and meeting other pups, who they could keep running with for hours.\n  - paws: Audrey pays attention to sensitive areas like ears and paws during gentle grooming, emphasizing patience and positivity.\n  - pup-friendly: And