oys working on cars, as music helps him focus and feel great while doing it. Calvin finds repairing things fulfilling, similar to Dave's satisfaction with car work.\n  - vintage Mustang: Dave is working on a Ford Mustang he found in a junkyard. He finds working on cars therapeutic to relax. Previously, he had worked on the engine, but heard a weird noise upon starting it.\n  - car stuff: Dave is tied up with car stuff, recently returned from San Francisco with knowledge on car modification. He listens to vinyl while working on cars to relax and stay productive.\n  - classic muscle car: Dave is working on a classic muscle car, modifying it to have a modern vibe while retaining its classic style. He is learning auto engineering for this project.\n  - dad: Dave's dad took him to his first car show when he was 10, which sparked his interest in cars. Dave later became an automotive engineer.\n  - Dave: Dave is fascinated by how machines work, starting at age ten after fixing an old car. He enjoys car engineering and transforming broken-down vehicles into high-running ones.\n  - car show: Dave's interest in cars began at age 10 when his dad took him to his first car show, leading him to become an automotive engineer.\n  - classic cars: Dave opened his car maintenance shop, fulfilling a dream. He works on all kinds of cars, including full restorations of classic cars.\n  - automotive engineer: Dave is an automotive engineer whose interest started at age 10 after attending a car show with his dad. He finds building powerful cars from small parts cool.\n  - Dave: Dave is restoring a Ford Mustang from a junkyard, working on car mods, and added a custom exhaust and performance upgrades to it. He attended a car show last Friday.\n  - cars: Dave shared a picture of his latest car project, which Calvin found inspiring, contrasting it with Calvin's music endeavors. Dave finds working on cars therapeutic.\n  - auto engineering: Dave's fascination with auto engineering started at ag