Caroline attended a pride parade last Friday, describing it as awesome with much energy and love, reinforcing the importance of equality.\n  - safe space: Caroline attended an LGBTQ+ counseling workshop last Friday where pros were passionate about making a safe space for trans people.\n  - my own journey: Caroline shared details of her transgender journey, including struggles and development since coming out and starting transition three years ago, at a school event to inspire others.\n  - Caroline's Web: Melanie read \"Charlotte's Web\" as a child and appreciated how it showed the impact of friendship and compassion.\n  - \"Brave\" by Sara Bareilles: Caroline finds \"Brave\" by Sara Bareilles significant as it represents courage and fighting for what is right, reminding her of her progress.\n  - identities: Identities were celebrated and shared through poetry at a transgender poetry reading, creating a safe and empowering space for self-expression.\n  - artist: Caroline, an artist, attended a pride parade last Friday and was asked by Melanie about how she stays inclusive in her work.\n  - inspiring stories: Caroline attended an LGBTQ support group yesterday and Melanie inquired about any inspiring stories heard there.\n  - kids in need: Melanie's kids made things with clay. Caroline attended a council meeting about adoption, which made her more determined to adopt children in need.\n  - transgender conference: Caroline attended an LGBTQ conference two days ago, met people with similar journeys, and felt accepted while learning about fighting for trans rights.\n  - LGBTQ conference: Caroline attended an LGBTQ conference two days ago, finding it special, welcoming, and connecting with people on similar journeys. She felt accepted and recognized the importance of fighting for trans rights.\n  - Sara Bareilles: Caroline mentioned the song \"Brave\" by Sara Bareilles, noting it is significant to her because it is about courage and fighting for what is right.\n  - book: 