rtner went scuba diving last Friday and found a cool spot to explore. Jolene also shared a picture of herself and her partner at a music festival last year.\n  - dive spot: Jolene and someone else tried a scuba diving lesson last Friday and found a cool dive spot they can explore together.\n  - Phuket: Jolene traveled to Phuket for a few weeks at a meditation retreat with her partner for nature, reflection, and a break from engineering studies. In Thailand, they tried a new style of meditation with flowers.\n  - lake: Jolene is attending a meditation course at a retreat near a lake. Previously, Jolene captured a photo of a lake surrounded by trees, noting its peacefulness.\n  - underwater life: Deborah expressed interest in underwater life after Jolene mentioned trying a scuba diving lesson.\n  - Walking Dead: Jolene and others are planning to play \"Walking Dead\" next Saturday.\n  - tips: Deborah offered tips to Jolene for yoga practice, and Jolene thanked her and said she would check them out.\n  - meditation: Jolene uses meditation for self-care, planning a camping trip. She recently tried a new style of meditation with flowers in Thailand.\n  - new poses: Jolene inquired about what new poses Deborah tried after Deborah expressed excitement about a milestone accomplishment.\n  - Jolene and Anna: Deborah mentioned Anna got her a tasty vegan stir-fry (tofu, veg, ginger, soy sauce). Jolene mentioned doing yoga and meditation last Friday for me-time.\n  - hobbies: Jolene is seeking tips for balancing hobbies and studies; Deborah focuses on teaching yoga and organizing a yoga event last month.\n  - things that bring you joy: Deborah advises Jolene to make time for 'things that bring you joy' to experience joy.\n  - Dancer Pose (Natarajasana): Deborah tried a new pose, Dancer Pose (Natarajasana), and asked Jolene for a rating.\n  - snakes: Jolene has snakes; they enjoy watching her relax and bring her a sense of calm.\n  - Avalanche: Jolene read \"Avalanche\" by Neal 