he future.\n  - videogame controller: Nate shared a photo of himself holding a videogame controller while congratulating Joanna on seeing her written work acted out for the third time.\n  - feedback: Joanna received positive feedback that people are connecting with her writing, which Nate mentioned.\n  - \"Finding Home\": \"Finding Home\" is a script Joanna is writing with her writers group about a girl's journey to find her true home. She finds the work rewarding and emotional.\n  - picture: Nate complimented Joanna's drawings, asking what inspired them. Joanna previously mentioned seeing her writing acted out and Nate complimented a hiking picture.\n  - doubt: Joanna expressed a 'tug-of-war of hope and doubt' after finishing her second script, feeling a mix of excitement and terror about her work getting noticed.\n  - Woodhaven: Joanna visited Woodhaven for a road trip; seeing how much the town changed sparked ideas for her next movie script. Woodhaven has an interesting past with cool people.\n  - old notebooks: Joanna found old notebooks containing her early writings last week, showing her progress. Nate asked Joanna what she was working on in that notebook.\n  - Rejections: Joanna received rejections from a film contest, which Nate acknowledged as tough but encouraged her to keep trying.\n  - Jo: Joanna (Jo) asked Nate if he celebrated good feedback people are connecting with his writing. Previously, she asked about a couple he met while walking Max.\n  - talent: Nate encouraged Joanna, affirming her incredible talent and promising her hard work will pay off. Joanna is using a road trip for research for her next movie.\n  - writer: Joanna, identified as a writer, experienced a major setback when her laptop crashed, resulting in the loss of all her work.\n  - Joanna: Joanna is filming her own movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - presentation: Joanna finished the presentation for movie pro