om: Deborah reconnected with her mom's old friends, and hearing stories about her mom was emotional, bringing a mix of happy and sad feelings, but overall comforting.\n  - plans for this day: Deborah has plans for this day, which caused her to cancel a previously discussed yoga getaway.\n  - Deb: Deborah (Deb) ran a free community gardening class yesterday with her neighbor, which was enjoyed by people of any age.\n  - one of the places: Deborah stated that 'one of the places' is a location where she spends time with family and cherishes memories, following her father's passing.\n  - activities: Deborah told Anna the story of her life last Friday. Deborah focuses on teaching yoga and organizing a yoga event last month. Jolene asked about maintaining balance between hobbies and studies.\n  - running group: Deborah started a running group with Anna; they help and push each other for motivation. Deborah has many photos from this activity.\n  - they: Deborah mentioned attending a community meetup where stories were shared, which made her think about relationships. Later, Deborah asked if 'they' taught something or if it was learned independently.\n  - destination: Deborah mentioned that the journey is as important as the destination, encouraging Jolene to take time for herself and find joy in it.\n  - journey: Deborah encourages Jolene's progress, emphasizing the importance of the journey, self-reflection, and personal joy alongside Jolene's engineering studies.\n  - little traditions: Deborah asked Jolene about any little traditions she has when reflecting on her mom.\n  - yoga retreat: Jolene attended an awesome yoga retreat described as peaceful with amazing sunrise views, making attendees feel alive and grateful. Deborah inquires about a future experience.\n  - Deborah's mother: Deborah's mother enjoyed reading and believed art could give strong emotions and uniquely connect people. Deborah feels close to her mother when visiting art shows.\n  - pendant: Anna has a 