d well, and were happy and safe.\n  - My dogs: Audrey's dogs enjoy meeting new people. They recently had grooming and look soft and fluffy.\n  - Pixie: Pixie is one of Audrey's four dogs, a Chihuahua mix, who curls up in her own bed to relax. Audrey is busy giving attention to her four dogs.\n  - tags: Audrey made personalized tags for her pets because she wants them to feel seen and loved.\n  - meadow: Andrew commented that dogs in a picture shared by Audrey look content, noting the meadow in the photo looks nice and brings joy to the pets.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - other pups: The dogs of Audrey love Fetch and Frisbee and enjoy running around and meeting other pups, who they could keep running with for hours.\n  - outdoors: Audrey misses taking her dogs for walks in nature, calling those moments with her pets in the outdoors chill and happy.\n  - groomers: Audrey took her pets to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; they looked cute with shiny coats and behaved well.\n  - exercise: Audrey pets and hugs her dog often for exercise and bonding. Audrey's dog, Precious, was scared, and Audrey calmed her by petting, hugging, and walking slowly.\n  - rewards: Audrey is looking forward to learning how to train her pets better and believes they will learn quickly because they love rewards.\n  - pets: Audrey bought dog toys last Monday. Andrew recently adopted a new puppy who is adjusting to his new home and getting along with Toby. Both find joy in pets.\n  - Audrey's dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; they looked cute with shiny coats and behaved well there.\n  - furry buddies: Andrew hopes Audrey and her furry buddies go on some fun adventures soon.\n  - her pups: One of Audrey's pups pulled so hard on the leash last Friday at the park that it busted; she chased and caught the pup. Audre