ese little guys' (turtles) for stress relief, describing them as small with big personalities. Joanna noted they looked serene and happy.\n  - them: Nate loves having 'them' around; they are cool, make him feel calm, don't require much looking after, and enjoy soaking in the sun.\n  - turtle: Joanna's script featured a turtle, and Nate mentioned getting a third turtle this year.\n  - Tampa: Nate took his turtles to the beach in Tampa yesterday, where they brought him peace.\n  - new tank: Nate got a new tank for his turtles because he bought another one; the tank is now large enough for three turtles.\n  - pets: Nate has new pets in a new tank and got them a friend. He previously took his pets to the park, finding moments with critters joyful.\n  - animals: Nate suggested Joanna write down things her animals like due to Joanna experiencing facial puffiness and itchiness around certain animals, causing avoidance.\n  - Nate: Nate enjoys the character Iron Man for his tech and humor. He keeps something in his room that reminds him to work on his goals. Previously, Nate enjoyed walking his dog Max and setting up dog playdates.\n  - favorites: Nate highly recommends something, stating the action scenes are awesome and the plot rocks, calling it one of his favorites.\n  - bookmark: Joanna finished a cute little bookmark for a lady at her writing club. Nate commented that the bookmark is great and she will love it.\n  - similar interests: Joanna and Nate established they have similar interests, leading Joanna to ask Nate about his preferred movie types.\n  - Nate: Nate made homemade coconut ice cream with sprinkles. His game tournament was postponed, and he didn't make the finals. He creates YouTube gaming content. He expressed support for Joanna filming her movie.\n  - Nate: Nate is an assistant who recently added a new family member named Max. He is communicating with Joanna about his busy week and Max.\n  - adventures: Nate likes a series described as having adventures,