last week and is motivated to help people. She also shared a photo reminding John that kindness matters.\n  - Maria: Maria met children at a shelter. She mentioned someone (unspecified) recently had to leave and find a new place due to tough circumstances.\n  - Maria: Maria is busy at the shelter preparing for a fundraiser next week to cover basic needs for the homeless; she needs help getting the word out about the chili cook-off at the event.\n  - Maria: Maria agrees with John about the importance of education for kids. She volunteers, inspired by her aunt who helped her family.\n  - Maria: Maria joined a gym last week, is sticking to her routine to get stronger and improve endurance, and is trying kundalini yoga. She recently met children at a shelter.\n  - Maria: Maria is an assistant who spoke with John about his visit to a veteran's hospital and the resilience of the veterans there.\n  - Maria: Maria apologized to John for a late reply, shared photos of children from a shelter, and thanked John for an offer to help.\n  - Maria: Maria is supportive of John's decision to run for office. She has recently been involved in rewarding charity work.\n  - Maria: Maria thinks it is sad that resource scarcity impacts children's dreams and found volunteering for them awesome. She asked John about a photo from his yoga class.\n  - Maria: Maria discussed the resilience of veterans, enjoyed a refreshing hike with supportive church friends last weekend, and exchanged encouraging words with John about his new job.\n  - Maria: Maria, an assistant, served meals at a charity event last Friday. She is currently taking a poetry class and asked John about his great yoga instructor.\n  - Maria: Maria expressed amazement at John joining the fire-fighting brigade and encouraged spreading kindness to bring joy and comfort to others.\n  - Maria: Maria reacted positively to John joining the fire-fighting brigade and commented on the inspiring community support for the local fire station.\